# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# camelot — the neutral teaching world that ships with dli.
#
# A recognizable, wholly public-domain setting (the Matter of Britain — King
# Arthur, Camelot, the Round Table) that exercises the full teaching surface end
# to end so a new author can learn dli without absorbing any one production
# world's private canon. It mirrors every shape the later lanes check: a
# totally-ordered era spine (>=3 eras) with a narration vantage, events with a
# before-fact and a deliberately UNORDERED pair, a place adjacency graph
# (>=6 edges), people, a thing, facts, states with since/until across two eras,
# a magic practice (a spoken enchantment) with a graded-monotone resource, and
# an open question and hypothesis. Provenance is this world's OWN decision list
# (d-0001..) — a solo writer's ledger, per 01-syntax §3.
scope camelot

use language          # the practice below consumes the language layer
use chronology        # ...and story-time, for the knowledge state a name earns

# --- the world's ledger: the decisions its citations rest on ------------------
# Declaring a decision is what lets `decided d-000n` carry authority rather than
# mint it (B1): a citation to an undeclared decision fails closed.
ratify d-0001
ratify d-0002
ratify d-0003
ratify d-0004
ratify d-0005
ratify d-0006
ratify d-0007
ratify d-0008
ratify d-0009   # the cyclic-time + ordering-rule extension
ratify d-0010   # the lexical ban
ratify d-0012   # lancelot's oath scene — the ground the worked proof rests on

# --- world chronology: a totally-ordered era spine (>=3 eras) -----------------
era uthers-time < arthurs-reign < after-camlann   decided d-0001

# events carry era membership; WITHIN an era only `before` orders them
event the-sword-drawn         during uthers-time     decided d-0002
event the-round-table-founded during arthurs-reign   decided d-0002
event the-grail-quest         during arthurs-reign   decided d-0003
event the-battle-of-camlann   during arthurs-reign   proposed

# a declared intra-era order:
before the-round-table-founded -> the-battle-of-camlann   decided d-0003
# ...and a DELIBERATELY UNORDERED pair: the-grail-quest shares arthurs-reign with
# the-round-table-founded but no before-fact orders them, so
# happens-before(the-grail-quest, the-round-table-founded) answers `unordered` —
# a first-class verdict, not a silent tie-break (03-time §1).

narration vantage after-camlann
# inert: the narrator looks back from after Camlann; declaring an event in the
# vantage era is a type error (03-time §1.iii).

# --- cyclic time: public-domain cycles a practice seats its hour on (03-time §1.iv)
# The moon's twenty-nine nights and the four seasons — cyclic kinds with no epoch
# and no calendar: succ/pred/across/distance exist, but `<`, sort, and max are
# type errors (a cycle refuses rank). The engine seats no ambient cycles; a world
# declares the ones its practices need — oath-binding seats its wrong-moon hour on
# `moon` below.
cycle moon(29)                                        decided d-0009
cycle season(4) = spring | summer | autumn | winter   decided d-0009

# --- an ordering rule over the era/event spine (03-time §6, block B) -----------
# A floor on when the deepest era may first be shown, held as data the season
# checker reads rather than as code. Inert until an episode season binds a
# production order to check it against — a declaration, not a running constraint.
rule uthers-time-held-back over order   decided d-0009
  : listener-learns(during uthers-time _) requires act > 1

# --- places and the adjacency graph (6 places, >=6 edges) ---------------------
place camelot        "Camelot"          decided d-0004
place the-lake       "The Lake"         decided d-0004
place avalon         "Avalon"           decided d-0004
place camlann        "Camlann"          decided d-0005
place tintagel       "Tintagel"         decided d-0005
place the-waste-land "The Waste Land"   decided d-0005

adjacent(camelot, the-lake)          decided d-0004
adjacent(camelot, camlann)           decided d-0004
adjacent(camelot, tintagel)          decided d-0005
adjacent(the-lake, avalon)           decided d-0005
adjacent(camlann, the-waste-land)    decided d-0005
adjacent(the-waste-land, avalon)     decided d-0005
adjacent(tintagel, the-lake)         proposed

# --- people, a thing, and facts -----------------------------------------------
person arthur    "Arthur, the King"   decided d-0006
person merlin    "Merlin"             decided d-0006
person guinevere "Guinevere"          decided d-0006
person lancelot  "Lancelot"           decided d-0007
person mordred   "Mordred"            decided d-0007
person morgan    "Morgan"             decided d-0007
thing excalibur  "Excalibur"          decided d-0008

fact arthur   rules    camelot        decided d-0006
fact merlin   counsels arthur         decided d-0006
fact lancelot serves   arthur         decided d-0007

# the certain ground the worked oath-binding proof (below) rests on: Lancelot's
# standing at court and the king's consent are facts in the certain layer, so the
# proof's premises seat in the pool rather than fizzle.
standing(lancelot)   decided d-0012
consent(arthur)      decided d-0012

# --- states: facts acquire validity spans (the two-era sword case) ------------
state excalibur.keeper = in-the-stone until the-sword-drawn   decided d-0008
state excalibur.keeper = the-king     since the-sword-drawn   decided d-0008
# in-the-stone UNTIL the sword is drawn and the-king's SINCE it: an interregnum
# flashback checks clean AND the reign checks clean, because the two claims hold
# over disjoint spans (03-time §2). No false contradiction between them.

# --- the magic layer: a spoken enchantment (04-practices §4) ------------------
# A dialect-derived true-name, the knowledge state that learning it initiates,
# and the practice that spends it — three layers meeting in one pack, zero kernel
# code, exactly as the practices workbench's acceptance test does.
dialect old-speech "the old speech"  proposed {
  basis attested "Old Welsh / Brythonic"   # an external-world claim (05 §1, §7):
                                           # the author ratifies the SOUND, never
                                           # the scholarship — never a support term
  vowels a e i o u y
  endings -a -oc -wen
  cluster-max 2
  stress penultimate
  name-kind person.given = given-proto given-deutero
  name-part myr "sea"           role given-proto    proposed
  name-part din "fastness"      role given-deutero  proposed
  }

name myrdin "Myrdin"  person.given in old-speech
  = given-proto myr + given-deutero din
  bearer the-enchanter   proposed
  # checked at compile: the slot sequence matches a name-kind pattern, each
  # name-part exists under its claimed role, and the composed form passes the
  # phonotactics. A mispronunciation IS a failed dialect derivation (L4 below).

# --- the lexicon: a cited lexical ban (05 §4) ---------------------------------
# The allegory-ban's public-domain shape: the register is kept period-true by a
# ruling, so an anachronism is a cited lexicon fact, not a config entry. No name
# or diegetic term may carry it.
banned cannon d-0010 "the Matter of Britain keeps to sword and spear — no gunpowder anachronism"

# --- a coined in-world term (05 §4) -------------------------------------------
# A `term` gives one of the world's own ideas a name, so a later claim can cite
# the term rather than re-gloss it each time. The freeing of the sword is such an
# idea: named once here (citing the sword's own decision), reusable everywhere
# after — the lexical counterpart to the `banned` ruling above.
term the-drawing "the freeing of Excalibur from the stone by the rightful king"  decided d-0008

# --- the agent-init flow: a proposal bundle under one hypothesis (05 §5) -------
# Candidate dialect data enters like world lore: proposed, under one hypothesis
# variable, every clause carrying agent provenance by inheritance. Composed
# through an unratified name-part, the name is merely-possible BY CONSTRUCTION —
# visible to shadow queries, structurally excluded from every context pack and
# assertion until the bundle is ruled. No ratify follows: this is a live proposal.
hypothesis h-old-loan "the old speech took a hero-name from the tongue over the water"

name-part tal "brow, high"  role given-proto  proposed agent:factory/naming-run-0714  assumes h-old-loan

name taldin "Taldin"  person.given in old-speech
  = given-proto tal + given-deutero din
  proposed agent:factory/naming-run-0714  assumes h-old-loan

event the-speaking-day   during arthurs-reign   proposed
state knows.caster.myrdin = true  since the-speaking-day   proposed
# learning a name is a knowledge state initiated when it is learned;
# query knows(caster, true-name(bearer)) as-of a scene (03-time §4).

practice merlins-craft  proposed {
  use language.registers                # its primitives ARE the naming layer
  resource breath(word) : graded monotone full > spent > silent
  rule speak(bearer) requires
      knows(caster, true-name(bearer)),
      breath(true-name(bearer)) >= spent,
      derivation(true-name(bearer)) checks in register-of(bearer)
  effect speak degrades breath by 1     # a word spoken thins the breath behind it
  condition unheard requires no witness within earshot
  error mis-spoken     refines L4 bad-instantiation
                       # a mispronunciation IS a failed dialect derivation
  error stale-name     refines L2 where premise-outdated
                       # the bearer has changed since the name was learned
  error word-overheard refines L3 side-condition [unheard] signals degrade(+1)
  cost vital | epistemic
  }

# --- a second practice: oath-binding, a linear-conserved debt (04-practices §3)
# A vow is a debt: the boon a swearer owes must balance across every close — a
# LINEAR CONSERVED resource, neither merlins-craft's graded-monotone decay nor an
# affine-only bound. It seats its hour on the `moon` cycle above, and its failures
# span the L2..L6 ladder INCLUDING the licensed-ignorance shape only this kernel
# can state: an oath that seats true against a licensed pool yet lies against the
# certain. Hosts on the one generic checker with zero per-practice kernel code.
practice oath-binding  proposed {
  use chronology.cycles                        # the pledge seats its hour on the moon
  kind bond = fealty | troth | ransom
  role oathgiver  : person   requires standing(oathgiver)
  role oathholder : person   requires consent(oathholder)
  resource boon   : linear conserved           # a boon owed must balance — the debt law
  resource strain : affine bounded body-limit  # the swearer's body caps the draw
  rule pledge(bond, oathgiver)
  rule give-and-take                           # every boon revealed, assigned, or released balances
  condition witnessed requires witness within earshot
  error unowed        refines L2 premise-not-available where absent
                      # a pledge drawn on a boon never granted
  error forsworn      refines L2 premise-not-available where contradicted signals dishonour
                      # a boon the ledger contradicts recoils on the swearer
  error wrong-moon    refines L3 side-condition [timing] over cycle moon
                      # the same oath, sworn at the wrong turn of the moon
  error overpledged   refines L6 resource-violation on strain signals collapse
                      # pledging more strain than the body-limit allows
  error hollow-vow    refines L2 where available-in(licensed-pool) and contradicted-in(certain)
                      # seats-and-lies: true against a licensed pool, false against the certain
  cost social | bodily | material | epistemic
  }

# --- a worked diegetic proof: one scene's reasoning, checked (04-practices §5) -
# A `proof` records a bounded piece of reasoning inside a practice: certain-layer
# premises, a resource drawn against one of them, the rule instantiated, a chain
# that concludes the close atom, the resource spent, and the atom it closes on.
# Lancelot swears fealty to Arthur — his standing and the king's consent seat in
# the pool; a boon is drawn against his standing; the `pledge` rule is
# instantiated; a `give-and-take` chain concludes the vow; the boon is spent so
# the linear-conserved debt balances to zero; and the close holds. The interior
# is captured clause text, checked by the proof lane against oath-binding, with
# zero kernel code.
proof lancelots-oath  speaker lancelot  in oath-binding {
  premise p1  standing(lancelot)  cited d-0012  cue "Lancelot comes to court"
  premise p2  consent(arthur)     cited d-0012
  premise p3  boon(1)             drawn-against p1
  step   s1  instantiate pledge  with bond = fealty, oathgiver = lancelot
  step   s2  chain from p1, s1 by give-and-take conclusion pledged(lancelot, fealty)
  spend  p3
  close  pledged(lancelot, fealty)  expect holds
  }

# --- the craft the practice serves, and the open fork it leaves ---------------
rule show-the-price over season  proposed
principle a-name-spends-breath   proposed

fork what-does-the-word-cost
  option a-year-of-life
  option a-truth-told

# --- an open fork: a question with options under a hypothesis ------------------
hypothesis h-return "Excalibur was always the Lake's to reclaim, never the king's to keep"

question who-holds-excalibur "Who holds Excalibur after Camlann?"
  option arthur   implies keeps(arthur, excalibur)
  option the-lake implies keeps(the-lake, excalibur)   assumes h-return
# proposed-first: neither option is canon until a ruling; the question is a
# tracked debt, not a blank (01-syntax §4).

# --- a settled hypothesis: the ratify BLOCK that turns a supposition certain ---
# The counterpart to h-old-loan's live proposal: a hypothesis the author HAS ruled
# on. A bare `ratify d-000n` (the ledger at the top) mints a decision; a ratify
# BLOCK additionally settles a named hypothesis — the claim that `assumes` it
# flips from merely-possible to certain in one recorded act (05 §5). This block
# also declares d-0011, so its citations carry authority like any ledger entry.
hypothesis h-merlin-foresaw "Merlin foresaw the fall at Camlann from the first"
event the-warning  during arthurs-reign  proposed assumes h-merlin-foresaw
ratify d-0011 { h-merlin-foresaw := true }
